// MsgPlaceOrder crosses against the book and rests what is left.
//
// # Escrow first, then fill
//
// The whole of the trader's side is escrowed before a single match is
// attempted: shares for an ask, money for a bid, at the trader's own limit.
// Every fill is then paid out of that escrow, and whatever is left over is
// either the remainder resting or a refund at the end.
//
// The alternative — fill from the trader's own balance and escrow only what
// rests — is one bank send shorter and wrong in a way that only shows up under
// load. It leaves a window inside the cross where the trader's balance is still
// theirs, so a fill part-way through the loop can fail for insufficient funds
// after earlier fills have already settled, and the handler is then holding
// half a trade.
//
// # Price improvement belongs to the taker
//
// A fill happens at the RESTING order's price, never the incoming one. The
// resting order named a price and waited; the incoming order accepted it. Where
// a bid crosses an ask below its limit, the difference is refunded to the
// bidder rather than paid to the seller — the seller asked for their price and
// got it, and a mechanism that quietly paid them more would be charging the
// taker for the privilege of having been patient.
type MsgPlaceOrder struct {
	Trader   string                `protobuf:"bytes,1,opt,name=trader,proto3" json:"trader,omitempty"`
	Denom    string                `protobuf:"bytes,2,opt,name=denom,proto3" json:"denom,omitempty"`
	Side     Side                  `protobuf:"varint,3,opt,name=side,proto3,enum=blockchain.market.v1.Side" json:"side,omitempty"`
	Quantity cosmossdk_io_math.Int `protobuf:"bytes,4,opt,name=quantity,proto3,customtype=cosmossdk.io/math.Int" json:"quantity"`
	// Settlement units per one share, and a limit rather than a target: a bid
	// will not pay more, an ask will not take less. There is no market order,
	// deliberately — on a book this thin an unpriced order is an instruction to
	// accept whatever single resting order happens to be there, which on a
	// vehicle with four holders is not a price.
	UnitPrice uint64 `protobuf:"varint,5,opt,name=unit_price,json=unitPrice,proto3" json:"unit_price,omitempty"`
}

